UNIT escape_data
KIND FUNCTIONAL
FIDELITY package
ANCHOR rederive@c509956a8f8a cli/lsp/pr-review.mjs escapeData, reproduced exactly. Independent anchor: GitHub's toolkit
  @actions/core@3.0.1 (lib/command.js escapeData, observed through core.error(message) with stdout captured, the text after
  "::error::"). On every TEXT argument the two agree (39899 of 39899 seeded and curated texts, R1-R5); they differ only on
  non-text values, which the pinned code renders by the host's generic text conversion and the toolkit by its own
  toCommandValue (a JSON rendering, none and absent -> empty). That difference is the ruling already made for the sibling
  unit escape_property: the pinned conversion is kept, and it lives in the js and ts language files.
ORACLE-CLASS deterministic
SIG escape_data(value: text) -> text
ENVELOPE text only: any length (including empty), any well-formed Unicode text. Text holding an unpaired surrogate half
  and non-text arguments are js widenings (see the js and ts files), not part of the abstract contract; R4 states that
  such halves pass through unchanged.
DEPENDS-ON none
DESCRIPTION Escape a text for use as the MESSAGE of a GitHub Actions workflow command (the part after the second "::" in
  "::error file=…::message"), so that the runner reads the whole text as one message and nothing in it can end the
  command line or start another command. Pull-request contract text flows into this; a missing escape is a
  workflow-command injection.
BEHAVIOR
R1 The result is the input with each character of ESCAPES replaced by its three-character escape, judged one code unit at
  a time in a single left-to-right pass. Every other code unit is copied unchanged in its original position; nothing is
  dropped, added or reordered.
R2 The percent sign is escaped, and it is escaped BEFORE (independently of) the escapes R1 inserts: the "%" that begins an
  inserted "%0D" or "%0A" is never escaped again. Equivalently each input character maps once, by ESCAPES.
R3 The operation is not idempotent: an input that already contains an escape sequence ("%0A", "%25") has its percent sign
  escaped again ("%250A", "%2525"). A carriage return and a line feed are escaped separately, so CR LF becomes "%0D%0A".
R4 Only the three characters of ESCAPES are escaped. Colon, comma, equals, "::", tab, the other ASCII controls (NUL, VT,
  FF), next line (U+0085), line and paragraph separators (U+2028, U+2029), non-ASCII letters, surrogate pairs and unpaired
  surrogate halves are all copied unchanged. CITED FIDELITY package — colon and comma are escaped by the sibling
  escape_property (a command PROPERTY value), not here; the toolkit's message escaping is the same three-character set.
R5 Empty text -> empty text.
TABLE ESCAPES — input character -> replacement (uppercase hex, the UTF-8 / ASCII code of the character)
  "%"  (U+0025 percent sign)    -> "%25"
  CR   (U+000D carriage return) -> "%0D"
  LF   (U+000A line feed)       -> "%0A"
INVARIANT length(result) = length(input) + 2 × (number of ESCAPES characters in input).
INVARIANT the result contains no CR and no LF, so it cannot end the workflow-command line.
NOTE rust is omitted. Cause: domain — the review system ships as JavaScript (rdv review and the rederive/sir-review GitHub
  Action); there is no Rust consumer.
ORACLE value -> oracles/escape_data.json  CANONICAL-SHA256 10910a115e2248977df0c494da7a5c6c95796049bbb455c03b673052b418678f
SCOPE IN: R1-R5 over any text. OUT: the workflow-command framing itself (the "::name props::" prefix, the annotations
  builder), property escaping (escape_property), the runner's unescaping, and the toolkit's toCommandValue conversion of
  non-text values (ruled out; see ANCHOR).
PROVENANCE rederive@c509956a8f8a (rederive, the review system), cli/lsp/pr-review.mjs line 120, named export escapeData;
